                    ("easy", "Why are most Actuator endpoints not exposed by default beyond health and info?",
                     "Many endpoints (env, threaddump, heapdump, and others) expose genuinely sensitive internal details - environment variables that may include secrets, full stack traces, memory contents - that shouldn't be reachable by an unauthenticated caller. Spring Boot only exposes health and info by default specifically to avoid accidentally leaking this information; anything else must be explicitly opted into via management.endpoints.web.exposure.include and should be properly secured in any real deployment."),
